    17→\added{\textbf{Data Acquisition Details.} Table~\ref{tab:acquisitions} summarises the satellite datasets and geographic coverage to support reproducibility. All Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 scenes are freely accessible from the ESA Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem}\footnotemark[1]; \added{GFSC composites are available from the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service HRWSI portal}\footnotemark[2]. \added{The raw data archive comprises 178 co-registered Sentinel-1/Sentinel-2 acquisition pairs (407\,GB total) collected from December 2024 to July 2025, spanning 45 MGRS tiles across Finland (60--70.5\textdegree{}N, 20--32\textdegree{}E, UTM zones 33--36) with a maximum Sentinel-2 cloud coverage threshold of 20\% applied at retrieval time. After quality-controlled preprocessing, including SAR radiometric calibration, terrain correction, optical atmospheric correction, and geometric co-registration, 28 W-band (northern Finland, 64--72\textdegree{}N) tiles with complete processing pipelines were retained for training data construction. Assembling the final dataset required temporally matching three independently scheduled data streams: Sentinel-1 (6-day revisit cycle), Sentinel-2 (5-day revisit cycle), and GFSC 7-day composites. Differences in revisit periods, orbital geometries, viewing angles, and composite dating windows substantially constrain the number of valid co-temporal combinations; after applying a strict 30-day temporal window for triplet alignment, 29 matched (S1, S2, GFSC) triplets from 19 unique W-band MGRS tiles were obtained. These triplets fall within the December 2024--July 2025 collection window, covering conditions from snow-free summer through autumn snow onset in northern Lapland, and together encompass the full range of fractional snow cover conditions (0--100\%) present in the dataset.}
