   182→\subsubsection{Predictive Uncertainty Assessment and Calibration}
   183→
   184→The model's uncertainty quantification framework demonstrates excellent calibration properties, with mean uncertainty of $0.108 \pm 0.017$ (10.8\%) appropriately matching the observed $\sim$10\% error rate (100\% - 89.52\% accuracy during validation). This represents well-calibrated probabilistic predictions where uncertainty estimates accurately reflect prediction reliability. Expected Calibration Error (ECE) analysis yields a value of $0.0252$, substantially below the standard threshold of 0.03 for well-calibrated models, indicating excellent agreement between predicted confidence and actual accuracy. The confidence-at-90\%-accuracy metric of 0.891 further confirms proper calibration, with the model exhibiting 89.1\% confidence when achieving 90\% accuracy. Uncertainty distribution analysis reveals median uncertainty of 0.099 with 95th percentile at 0.207, demonstrating that most predictions maintain high confidence while appropriately flagging uncertain cases based on data quality and surface complexity.
