   352→\textbf{R2-4: Data acquisition dates for reproducibility}
   353→\begin{quote}
   354→\textit{``The paper mentions Northern Finland during winter 2025 and citations include 2025 papers. [...] The authors should ensure the specific dates of acquisition are listed to ensure reproducibility.''}
   355→\end{quote}
   356→We thank the reviewer for this important reproducibility concern. We have added Table~2 (Section~4.1) with a full dataset summary, and we correct a labelling error in Sections~4.4 and~6 where the manuscript erroneously referred to ``winter 2025''; the dataset covers \textbf{December 2024 -- July 2025}, spanning the snow-free summer through the autumn snow-onset transition in northern Lapland. We apologise for this confusion.
   357→
   358→\textbf{Dataset provenance (three-stage pipeline).} The data collection proceeded in three stages, and we describe all three to give the reviewer the full picture:
   359→
   360→\begin{enumerate}
   361→  \item \textbf{Raw archive.} We downloaded a raw archive of \textbf{178 co-registered Sentinel-1/Sentinel-2 acquisition pairs} (407\,GB total) from the ESA Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem (\url{https://dataspace.copernicus.eu}), spanning \textbf{December 2024 to July 2025} across \textbf{45 MGRS tiles} in Finland (60--70.5\textdegree{}N, 20--32\textdegree{}E, UTM zones 33--36), with a Sentinel-2 maximum cloud coverage filter of 20\% applied at retrieval time.
   362→
   363→  \item \textbf{Quality-controlled preprocessing.} After radiometric calibration, terrain correction (SAR), atmospheric correction (optical), and geometric co-registration, \textbf{28 W-band tiles} (northern Finland, 64--72\textdegree{}N) with complete preprocessing pipelines were retained. The geographic focus on W-band tiles reflects the snow-monitoring objective and the availability of GFSC reference coverage for those tiles; V-band and other tiles were retained in the raw archive but not carried through the full preprocessing chain.
   364→
   365→  \item \textbf{Triplet matching.} Constructing training samples required assembling temporally coherent \textit{triplets} of co-located Sentinel-1, Sentinel-2, and GFSC acquisitions. This step is non-trivial: Sentinel-1 has a 6-day revisit cycle, Sentinel-2 a 5-day cycle, and GFSC products are 7-day gap-filled composites with their own composite dating windows. Differences in revisit periods, orbital geometries, and composite dating substantially reduce the number of valid co-temporal combinations. After applying a strict 30-day temporal alignment window, \textbf{29 matched (S1, S2, GFSC) triplets} from \textbf{19 unique W-band MGRS tiles} were obtained and used for training, validation, and testing.
   366→\end{enumerate}
   367→
   368→The 29 triplets span \textbf{Dec 2024--July 2025}, covering the transition from snow-free summer conditions through autumn snow onset in northern Lapland, and together represent the full 0--100\% fractional snow cover range in the dataset. GFSC composites are available from the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service HRWSI portal (\url{https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/snow}). The revised Table~2 (Section~4.1) summarises each sensor's key parameters and archive scope to support direct archive retrieval.
   369→
   370→\textit{Changes in manuscript:} Added Table~2 (sensor parameters and archive scope) and revised ``Data Acquisition Details'' paragraph in Section~4.1 with the three-stage provenance description; corrected ``northern Finland winter 2025'' $\rightarrow$ ``northern Finland (December 2024 -- July 2025)'' in Sections~4.4 and~6.
